```java
sealed interface PaymentMethod permits CreditCard, PayPal {}
record CreditCard(String cardNumber) implements PaymentMethod {}
record PayPal(String email) implements PaymentMethod {}

public class InstanceofDemo {
    static String describe(PaymentMethod p) {
        // Pattern matching for instanceof: checks AND casts in one step
        if (p instanceof CreditCard card) {
            return "Card ending " + card.cardNumber();
        } else if (p instanceof PayPal pp) {
            return "PayPal " + pp.email();
        }
        return "Unknown";
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(describe(new CreditCard("4111")));
        Object o = null;
        System.out.println(o instanceof String); // false, never throws on null
    }
}
```
`null instanceof X` is always false, so instanceof also guards against NullPointerException.

```java
class Notifier {
    // OVERLOADING: same name, different params, resolved at COMPILE time
    void send(String msg) { System.out.println("text: " + msg); }
    void send(String msg, int retries) { System.out.println(msg + " x" + retries); }

    String channel() { return "generic"; } // base behavior
}

class EmailNotifier extends Notifier {
    // OVERRIDING: same signature in a subclass, resolved at RUNTIME
    @Override String channel() { return "email"; }
}

public class OverloadVsOverrideDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Notifier n = new EmailNotifier();
        n.send("hi");        // overloading: compiler picks send(String)
        n.send("hi", 3);     // overloading: compiler picks send(String,int)
        System.out.println(n.channel()); // overriding: prints "email" (object type)
    }
}
```
Overloading is chosen by the compiler from argument types; overriding is chosen by the JVM from the actual object.

```java
abstract class ShippingMethod {
    abstract double calculateCost(double weight);
    abstract String getEstimatedDays();
}

class StandardShipping extends ShippingMethod {
    double calculateCost(double weight) {
        return weight * 5.0; // runtime: this version runs for StandardShipping objects
    }

    String getEstimatedDays() {
        return "5-7 business days";
    }
}

class ExpressShipping extends ShippingMethod {
    double calculateCost(double weight) {
        return weight * 15.0; // runtime: this version runs for ExpressShipping objects
    }

    String getEstimatedDays() {
        return "1-2 business days";
    }
}

void processOrder(Order order, ShippingMethod shipping) { // parent reference
    double cost = shipping.calculateCost(order.weight()); // JVM dispatches to actual object's method
    System.out.println("Cost: $" + cost + ", ETA: " + shipping.getEstimatedDays());
}

void main() {
    var order = new Order(123L, 2.5);
    processOrder(order, new StandardShipping()); // Output: Cost: $12.5, ETA: 5-7 business days
    processOrder(order, new ExpressShipping());  // Output: Cost: $37.5, ETA: 1-2 business days
    // Same processOrder code, different behavior based on actual object type
}
```

